# Atlas web — environment (example). Copy to `.env.local` for local overrides.
# `.env*` is gitignored; ONLY this `.env.example` is committed (CLAUDE.md § 4).
#
# HARD GATE (ADR-001 / ADR-006): the map renders KEYLESS by default. A fresh
# checkout with NO env file renders the self-hosted Protomaps `.pmtiles` basemap
# + the fleet on it, under a same-origin-only CSP. NOTHING below is required.

# --- Site URL (metadata / canonical). Falls back to the dev origin (port 3093).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://atlas.example.com

# --- OPTIONAL map enrichment (NOT required; the keyless basemap is the default).
# If you supply a tile/style key from a provider (e.g. a free MapTiler / Stadia
# tier), the map can use a richer vector style. Leaving these UNSET keeps the
# keyless self-hosted `.pmtiles` basemap and the tightest (same-origin) CSP.
#
# When you set a key, you MUST also set NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_HOST to the tile
# host so the CSP `connect-src`/`img-src` allow it (next.config.ts reads it).
# With no key, no external host is allowed — the keyless gate stays intact.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_HOST=https://tiles.example.com

# --- Telemetry WebSocket origin (Phase 4). Defaults to same-origin in dev.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=
